  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure C.2: \"Proportion Correct Cascades for 1000 Agents\". The same pair at the large-population end, and the separation is at its widest: \"our subsidy\" is already at about 0.98 at signal strength 0.5 and at 1.0 from 0.6 onward, while \"no subsidy\" starts at about 0.53 and climbs through 0.70, 0.87 and 0.95 before converging near 0.9. Set beside Figure C.1 and Figure 6.1 (100 agents), the three make one point the individual figures do not: the subsidy's benefit GROWS with population size.",
